IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-3-punishments`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 5 -- Abetment`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 107, 108, 108A, 108B, 109, 110, 111, 112, 113, 114, 115, 116, 117,
-- 118, 119, 120.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 107 -- Abetment of the doing of a thing`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 107(1)"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets the doing of a thing` IF
        ab's `instigates any person to do the thing`
    OR  (    ab's `engages with one or more other persons in a conspiracy for the doing of the thing`
         AND ab's `an act or illegal omission takes place in pursuance of that conspiracy and in order to the doing of that thing`)
    OR  ab's `intentionally aids by any act or illegal omission the doing of the thing`

-- s 107(2): a person may abet despite facts of which he is unaware which make
-- the doing of the thing impossible. The impossibility flag is not a precondition.

§§ `Section 108 -- Abettor`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108"
@export Decide whether the person abets an offence under Penal Code 1871 sections 107 and 108
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc Instigation, conspiracy (with an act or illegal omission in pursuance), or intentional aiding. The thing abetted must be an offence or would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor. Impossibility unknown to the abettor does not prevent abetment (s 107(2)).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets an offence` IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND ab's `the thing would be an offence if committed by a person capable of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as the abettor`

§§ `Section 108A -- Abetment in Singapore of an offence outside Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108A"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- s 108A does not require that the act abetted be an offence where it is to be done.
-- It requires only that the act, if committed in Singapore, would constitute an
-- offence. So the test is the s 107 abetment conduct plus the two location facts
-- plus that Singapore-referred criminality, and not the s 108 capable-person test.

DECIDE `the person abets an offence outside Singapore from Singapore` IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND ab's `the abetment takes place in Singapore`
    AND ab's `the act abetted would be committed outside Singapore`
    AND ab's `the act abetted would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore`

§§ `Section 108B -- Abetment outside Singapore of an offence in Singapore`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 108B"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person abets an offence in Singapore from outside Singapore` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence abetted would be committed in Singapore`
    AND ab's `any or all of the acts constituting the abetment were done outside Singapore`

§§ `Sections 109 and 110 -- Punishment of abetment where the act abetted is committed`

-- s 109: where the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment, and
-- this Code makes no express provision for the punishment of the abetment, the
-- abettor is punished with the punishment provided for the offence. The Explanation
-- says when an act is committed "in consequence" -- in consequence of the
-- instigation, in pursuance of the conspiracy, or with the aid which constituted
-- the abetment -- and that is the wording of the consequence fact. The Illustrations
-- are the bribe accepted (s 161 abetted), the false evidence given, and the
-- poisoning by conspiracy, where A is liable to the punishment for murder.
--
-- s 110: where the person abetted does the act with a different intention or
-- knowledge from the abettor's, the abettor is punished with the punishment for the
-- offence that would have been committed had the act been done with HIS intention
-- or knowledge and no other. The caller supplies that offence's punishment.
--
-- Both are encoded as an applicability test and a punishment. The punishment is the
-- one the caller supplies for the offence: the Code says "the punishment provided
-- for the offence" and nothing more, and the rule says the same.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 109"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 109 governs the punishment of the abetment
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. s 108 abetment, the act abetted committed in consequence of the instigation, conspiracy or aid, and no express provision for the punishment of the abetment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 109 applies to the abetment` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment`
    AND NOT ab's `express provision is made by this Code or by any other written law for the punishment of the abetment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 109"
@export Give the punishment of the abettor under Penal Code 1871 section 109, the punishment provided for the offence abetted
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment provided for the offence abetted.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 109 punishment of the abettor` ab p IS
    IF `section 109 applies to the abetment` ab THEN p ELSE `no punishment prescribed`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 110"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 110 governs the punishment of the abetment
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. s 108 abetment, and the person abetted doing the act with a different intention or knowledge from the abettor's.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 110 applies to the abetment` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the person abetted does the act with a different intention or knowledge from that of the abettor`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 110"
@export Give the punishment of the abettor under Penal Code 1871 section 110, the punishment for the offence that would have been committed with the abettor's own intention or knowledge
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment provided for the offence which would have been committed had the act been done with the abettor's intention or knowledge and no other.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 110 punishment of the abettor` ab p IS
    IF `section 110 applies to the abetment` ab THEN p ELSE `no punishment prescribed`

§§ `Section 111 -- Liability of the abettor when a different act is done`

-- When an act is abetted and a different act is done, the abettor is liable for the
-- act done in the same manner, and to the same extent, as if he had directly abetted
-- it, provided the act done was a probable consequence of the abetment and was
-- committed under the influence of the instigation, or with the aid or in pursuance
-- of the conspiracy which constituted the abetment.
--
-- The proviso carries the whole weight of the section, and both of its limbs are
-- required: Illustration (b) is the case that fails. A instigates B to burn Z's
-- house; B burns it and also steals from it. A is not liable for the theft, because
-- the theft was a distinct act and not a probable consequence of the burning.
-- Illustration (c) is the case that succeeds: instigating a midnight housebreaking
-- with arms, where the housebreakers murder a resident who resists.
--
-- s 111 presupposes an abetment, so the s 107 conduct test is conjoined. What it
-- does not require is that the thing abetted satisfy s 108: the section fixes the
-- abettor with the act actually done, not with the one he had in mind.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 111"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 111 fixes the abettor with a different act from the one abetted
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. Needs s 107 abetment conduct, a different act actually done, and both limbs of the proviso -- probable consequence, and done under the influence of the instigation or with the aid or in pursuance of the conspiracy.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abettor is liable under section 111 for the different act done` IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND ab's `a different act from the act abetted was done`
    AND ab's `the act done was a probable consequence of the abetment`
    AND ab's `the act done was committed under the influence of the instigation or with the aid or in pursuance of the conspiracy which constituted the abetment`

§§ `Section 112 -- Cumulative punishment for the act abetted and the act done`

-- Where the s 111 act is committed in addition to the act abetted and constitutes a
-- distinct offence, the abettor is liable to punishment for each. The Illustration:
-- A instigates B to resist a distress by force; B resists and also causes grievous
-- hurt to the officer; if A knew grievous hurt was likely, A is liable for both.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 112"
@export Decide whether the abettor is liable to cumulative punishment for the act abetted and the different act done under Penal Code 1871 section 112
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. s 111 liability for the different act, and that act being committed in addition to the act abetted and constituting a distinct offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abettor is liable to cumulative punishment under section 112` IF
        `the abettor is liable under section 111 for the different act done` ab
    AND ab's `the act for which the abettor is liable under section 111 is committed in addition to the act abetted and constitutes a distinct offence`

§§ `Section 113 -- Liability of the abettor for a different effect caused`

-- When an act is abetted with the intention on the part of the abettor of causing a
-- particular effect, and an act for which the abettor is liable in consequence of
-- the abetment causes a different effect from that intended, the abettor is liable
-- for the effect caused in the same manner, and to the same extent, as if he had
-- abetted the act with the intention of causing that effect, provided he knew that
-- the act abetted was likely to cause that effect.
--
-- s 111 is about a different ACT; s 113 is about a different EFFECT of an act for
-- which the abettor is already liable. The knowledge proviso is what distinguishes
-- s 113 from strict attribution: the Illustration is A instigating grievous hurt to
-- Z, Z dying, and A being liable for murder only if A knew the grievous hurt abetted
-- was likely to cause death.
--
-- "an act for which the abettor is liable in consequence of the abetment" reaches
-- both the act abetted itself and a s 111 act, so this test conjoins the s 107
-- conduct rather than either of the narrower predicates.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 113"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 113 fixes the abettor with an effect different from the one he intended
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. Needs s 107 abetment conduct, an intention to cause a particular effect, a different effect actually caused by an act for which the abettor is liable, and the abettor's knowledge that the act abetted was likely to cause that effect.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abettor is liable under section 113 for the different effect caused` IF
        `the person abets the doing of a thing` ab
    AND ab's `the act was abetted with the intention on the part of the abettor of causing a particular effect`
    AND ab's `an act for which the abettor is liable in consequence of the abetment causes a different effect from that intended`
    AND ab's `the abettor knew that the act abetted was likely to cause that effect`

§§ `Section 114 -- Abettor present when the offence is committed`

-- Whenever any person who, if absent, would be liable to be punished as an abettor
-- is present when the act or offence for which he would be punishable in consequence
-- of the abetment is committed, he is deemed to have committed such act or offence.
--
-- s 114 converts abetment into principal liability on the single added fact of
-- presence. The opening words -- "who, if absent, would be liable to be punished as
-- an abettor" -- are the whole of the abetment liability, so the test disjoins the
-- s 108 abettor and the s 111 abettor rather than naming only the first.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 114"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 114 deems an abettor present at the commission to have committed the act or offence himself
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. Needs liability as an abettor -- under ss 107 and 108, or under s 111 -- together with the abettor's presence when the act or offence was committed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abettor is deemed to have committed the act or offence under section 114` IF
        (   `the person abets an offence` ab
         OR `the abettor is liable under section 111 for the different act done` ab)
    AND ab's `the abettor was present when the act or offence for which he would be punishable was committed`

§§ `Sections 115 to 117 -- Punishment of abetment where the offence is not committed, and abetment of the public`

-- s 115: abetting an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life, where
-- the offence is NOT committed in consequence and no express provision is made for
-- the abetment's punishment: up to 20 years, and liable to fine or caning. The
-- Illustration is instigating a murder that is not committed.
-- s 116: the same for an offence punishable with imprisonment: punished as if the
-- abettor had committed the offence, except that by s 116(2) a fixed, specified
-- minimum or mandatory minimum sentence does not bind the court, which may pass any
-- sentence up to the maximum. s 116(3): no type of punishment not prescribed for the
-- offence. The rule takes the offence's punishment and strips its minimums.
-- s 117: abetting the commission of an offence by the public generally or by more
-- than 10 persons: up to 5 years, or fine, or both. The Illustration is a placard
-- at a worksite of more than 10 instigating the workers to damage property.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 115"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 115 governs the punishment of the abetment of an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life that is not committed
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. s 108 abetment of an offence punishable with death or life, not committed in consequence, with no express provision for the abetment's punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 115 applies to the abetment` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence abetted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    AND NOT ab's `the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment`
    AND NOT ab's `express provision is made by this Code or by any other written law for the punishment of the abetment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 115"
@export Give the punishment under Penal Code 1871 section 115 for abetting an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life that is not committed
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 115 punishment of the abettor` ab IS
    IF `section 115 applies to the abetment` ab
    THEN `imprisonment up to and liable to fine or caning or both` 20
    ELSE `no punishment prescribed`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 116"
@export Decide whether Penal Code 1871 section 116 governs the punishment of the abetment of an offence punishable with imprisonment that is not committed
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts. s 108 abetment of an offence punishable with imprisonment, not committed in consequence, with no express provision for the abetment's punishment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 116 applies to the abetment` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence abetted is punishable with imprisonment`
    AND NOT ab's `the act abetted is committed in consequence of the abetment`
    AND NOT ab's `express provision is made by this Code or by any other written law for the punishment of the abetment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 116"
@export Give the punishment under Penal Code 1871 section 116 for abetting an offence punishable with imprisonment that is not committed, the offence's own punishment without its minimums
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The abetment facts.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment prescribed for the offence abetted. Its fixed, specified minimum or mandatory minimum sentence does not bind (s 116(2)).
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 116 punishment of the abettor` ab p IS
    IF `section 116 applies to the abetment` ab THEN `with no minimum sentence` p ELSE `no punishment prescribed`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 117"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes abetting the commission of an offence by the public or by more than 10 persons under Penal Code 1871 section 117
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc s 108 abetment where what is abetted is the commission of an offence by the public generally or by a number or class of persons exceeding 10.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes abetting an offence by the public or by more than 10 persons` IF
        `the person abets an offence` ab
    AND ab's `abets the commission of an offence by the public generally or by any number or class of persons exceeding 10`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 117"
@export Give the punishment for abetting the commission of an offence by the public or by more than 10 persons under Penal Code 1871 section 117
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment for abetting an offence by the public` MEANS `imprisonment up to or fine or both` 5

§§ `Sections 118 to 120 -- Concealing a design to commit an offence`

-- Three offences with one shape. Intending to facilitate, or knowing it likely that
-- he will facilitate, the commission of an offence, the person voluntarily conceals
-- by act or illegal omission the existence of a design to commit it, or makes a
-- representation he knows to be false about the design. They differ in the offence
-- designed and the person: one punishable with death or life (s 118), one a public
-- servant has a duty to prevent (s 119), one punishable with imprisonment (s 120).
-- Each punishes more heavily if the offence is committed. The s 118 Illustration is
-- a false report to the police that a gang-robbery will be at C when it will be at
-- B; the s 119 Illustration is a police officer bound to report robbery designs who
-- omits to.
--
-- The punishments are computed. s 118 is fixed terms; ss 119 and 120 are fractions
-- of the longest term provided for the offence designed, with its fine, and s 119
-- substitutes fixed terms where that offence carries death or life.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 118 to 120"
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person conceals a design to commit an offence` IF
        ab's `intends to facilitate or knows it to be likely that he will thereby facilitate the commission of an offence`
    AND ab's `voluntarily conceals by any act or illegal omission the existence of a design to commit that offence or makes any representation which he knows to be false respecting that design`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 118"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life under Penal Code 1871 section 118
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc Concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life, or making a false representation about it, intending or knowing it likely to facilitate the offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes concealing a design to commit a capital or life offence` IF
        `the person conceals a design to commit an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence designed is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 118"
@export Give the punishment for concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life under Penal Code 1871 section 118
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The concealment facts. Up to 7 years if the offence is committed, 3 if not; fine in either case.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 118 punishment` ab IS
    IF ab's `the offence designed is committed`
    THEN `imprisonment up to and liable to fine` 7
    ELSE `imprisonment up to and liable to fine` 3

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 119"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a public servant concealing a design to commit an offence which it is his duty to prevent under Penal Code 1871 section 119
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc A public servant whose duty it is to prevent the offence designed, concealing the design or making a false representation about it, intending or knowing it likely to facilitate the offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a public servant concealing a design to commit an offence he must prevent` IF
        `the person conceals a design to commit an offence` ab
    AND ab's `is a public servant whose duty as such it is to prevent the commission of the offence designed`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 119"
@export Give the punishment for a public servant concealing a design to commit an offence he must prevent under Penal Code 1871 section 119
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The concealment facts.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment provided for the offence designed.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 119 punishment` ab p IS
    IF ab's `the offence designed is punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    THEN (IF ab's `the offence designed is committed`
          THEN `imprisonment up to and liable to fine` 15
          ELSE `imprisonment up to and liable to fine` 7)
    ELSE (IF ab's `the offence designed is committed`
          THEN `a fraction of the longest term provided for the offence with its fine` (1 DIVIDED BY 2) p
          ELSE `a fraction of the longest term provided for the offence with its fine` (1 DIVIDED BY 4) p)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 120"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment under Penal Code 1871 section 120
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc Concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment, or making a false representation about it, intending or knowing it likely to facilitate the offence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` IF
        `the person conceals a design to commit an offence` ab
    AND ab's `the offence designed is punishable with imprisonment`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 120"
@export Give the punishment for concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment under Penal Code 1871 section 120
GIVEN ab IS AN Abetment @desc The concealment facts.
      p IS A Punishment @desc The punishment provided for the offence designed.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the section 120 punishment` ab p IS
    IF ab's `the offence designed is committed`
    THEN `a fraction of the longest term provided for the offence with its fine` (1 DIVIDED BY 4) p
    ELSE `a fraction of the longest term provided for the offence with its fine` (1 DIVIDED BY 8) p

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes abetment of an offence` IF
        `the person abets an offence` (a's `abetment`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence` IF
        (   `constitutes concealing a design to commit a capital or life offence` (a's `abetment`)
         OR `constitutes a public servant concealing a design to commit an offence he must prevent` (a's `abetment`)
         OR `constitutes concealing a design to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment` (a's `abetment`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

